{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class B {\n    private static final long MOD = 998244353;\n\n    private static long modPow(long base, long exp) {\n        base %= MOD;\n        long res = 1;\n        for (; exp > 0; exp >>= 1) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) res = (res * base) % MOD;\n            base = (base * base) % MOD;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    private static long inv2() {\n        return modPow(2, MOD - 2);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        InputReader in = new InputReader(System.in);\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(new BufferedOutputStream(System.out));\n\n        long n = in.nextLong();\n        long m = in.nextLong();\n        long l = in.nextLong();\n        long r = in.nextLong();\n\n        long len = (r - l + 1) % MOD;\n        long total = n * m;\n\n        if ((n & 1) == 1 && (m & 1) == 1) {\n            out.println(modPow(len, total));\n        } else {\n            long p = modPow(len, total - 1);\n            long ans;\n            if (len % 2 == 0) {\n                ans = p * ((len / 2) % MOD) % MOD;\n            } else {\n                long oddCount = (len + 1) / 2;\n                long evenCount = (len - 1) / 2;\n                long part1 = p * oddCount % MOD;\n                long part2 = (p - 1 + MOD) % MOD * inv2() % MOD;\n                ans = (part1 - part2 + MOD) % MOD;\n            }\n            out.println(ans);\n        }\n\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    static class InputReader {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        InputReader(InputStream is) {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(is), 32768);\n        }\n\n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreTokens()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    throw new RuntimeException(e);\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() { return Long.parseLong(next()); }\n        int nextInt() { return Integer.parseInt(next()); }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport math\n\nMOD = 998244353\n\ndef mod_pow(base, exp):\n    base %= MOD\n    res = 1\n    while exp > 0:\n        if exp & 1 == 1:\n            res = (res * base) % MOD\n        base = (base * base) % MOD\n        exp >>= 1\n    return res\n\ndef inv2():\n    return mod_pow(2, MOD - 2)\n\nclass InputReader:\n    def __init__(self, is_stream):\n        self.br = sys.stdin\n        self.st = []\n        self.pos = 0\n    \n    def next(self):\n        while self.pos >= len(self.st):\n            line = self.br.readline()\n            if not line:\n                raise EOFError()\n            self.st = line.split()\n            self.pos = 0\n        token = self.st[self.pos]\n        self.pos += 1\n        return token\n    \n    def nextLong(self):\n        return int(self.next())\n    \n    def nextInt(self):\n        return int(self.next())\n\ndef main():\n    input_reader = InputReader(sys.stdin)\n    \n    n = input_reader.nextLong()\n    m = input_reader.nextLong()\n    l = input_reader.nextLong()\n    r = input_reader.nextLong()\n    \n    len_seg = (r - l + 1) % MOD\n    total = n * m\n    \n    if (n & 1) == 1 and (m & 1) == 1:\n        print(mod_pow(len_seg, total))\n    else:\n        p = mod_pow(len_seg, total - 1)\n        if len_seg % 2 == 0:\n            ans = p * ((len_seg // 2) % MOD) % MOD\n        else:\n            odd_count = (len_seg + 1) // 2\n            even_count = (len_seg - 1) // 2\n            part1 = p * odd_count % MOD\n            part2 = (p - 1 + MOD) % MOD * inv2() % MOD\n            ans = (part1 - part2 + MOD) % MOD\n        print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        main()\n    except EOFError:\n        pass\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.9828242481453344e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -0.0008531744824722409, -0.007677807472646236, -0.00462106429040432, -0.0009815642843022943, -0.28185683488845825, -0.00015877417172305286, -0.004295290447771549, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -4.529942543740617e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.1576648578047752e-05, -2.4318398573086597e-05, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -2.145764938177308e-06, -3.3378044463461265e-05, -7.033323527139146e-06, -0.033705245703458786, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -8.702239938429557e-06, -1.0490362910786644e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00030524839530698955, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, -0.004620589315891266, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1324817933200393e-05, -8.583032467868179e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07,